NAME
       fb_info, fb_blit, fb_acquire, fb_release - framebuffer access

SYNOPSIS
       #include <sys/cervus.h>

       int cervus_fb_info(cervus_fb_info_t *info);
       int cervus_fb_blit(const void *px, int x, int y, int w, int h);
       int cervus_fb_acquire(void);
       int cervus_fb_release(void);
       int cervus_fb_map(uint64_t *out_addr);

DESCRIPTION
       Draws to the screen from user space. fb_info reports the width,
       height, pitch and bit depth.

       Pixels handed to fb_blit are always 32-bit; the kernel converts
       to the native depth, so 24-bit and 16-bit modes need no special
       handling in the caller.

       fb_map maps the framebuffer straight into the address space and
       returns its address, for a program that would rather write
       pixels itself than hand them over a syscall.

       fb_acquire takes the screen for exclusive use, stopping the
       console from drawing over it, and fb_release gives it back.
       A program that only paints part of the screen, such as a preview
       pane beside text, can blit without acquiring.

RETURN VALUE
       0 on success, negative on failure.

SEE ALSO
       img(1), cfm(1), fbdemo(1)
